<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<jmeterTestPlan version="1.2" properties="5.0" jmeter="5.6.3">
  <hashTree>
    <TestPlan guiclass="TestPlanGui" testclass="TestPlan" testname="bng project list baseline">
      <stringProp name="TestPlan.comments">Baseline perf test for the project-LIST endpoints, ahead of BMD-933.

Both list handlers currently .select() every column with no projection and no
limit/offset, so each visible project ships its ENTIRE `project` JSONB document
(baseline + post-intervention) even though the list view needs only id, name,
createdAt, updatedAt. Response size = (projects visible) x (doc size), and both
factors are uncapped. This plan RECORDS that "before" state so the fix can be
shown to flatten it:
  * bytes  — the headline metric. Pre-fix it grows ~linearly with parcels/baseline;
             post-fix the acceptance criteria say it must be flat. JMeter's
             Summary Report saves the `bytes` column for free.
  * latency — the synchronous JSON.stringify of multi-MB rows is an event-loop
             stall; a concurrency run surfaces the p95/p99 knee and any 5xx.

Targets the BACKEND (:3001 local / bng-metric-backend.&lt;env&gt;.cdp-int.defra.cloud).
Both endpoints require a Defra ID bearer token — supplied WITHOUT touching the
command line (so CDP's `set -x` cannot log it) via ${__env(TOKEN)}, with a
-Jtoken override for local dry-runs.

setUp thread group seeds `seedProjects` projects, each carrying a baseline of
`seedParcels` synthetic parcels, via POST /projects/new. Seeded rows are only
visible to the SAME token/org that created them, so seed and measure with one
token. Set seedProjects=0 to skip seeding and measure a pre-populated dataset.

Because a single token sees ALL its visible projects at once, you sweep the two
size dimensions by RE-RUNNING with different seed params and comparing the
recorded bytes/latency — e.g.
  size sweep:  fix seedProjects, vary seedParcels  (100, 500, 1000, 2000)
  count sweep: fix seedParcels,  vary seedProjects (1, 10, 50, 100)
  concurrency: large seeded set, then crank threads/rampSeconds (the self-DoS risk)

Runtime properties (all overridable, -J..., or the CDP env var in brackets):
  token          Defra ID id_token bearer            (env TOKEN)          [never commit]
  userId         path segment for the /users route   (env USER_ID)        default perf-user
  seedProjects   projects to create in setUp; 0=skip (env SEED_PROJECTS)  default 10
  seedParcels    baseline parcels per seeded project (env SEED_PARCELS)   default 500
  threads        concurrent virtual users            (env THREAD_COUNT)   default 1
  rampSeconds    ramp-up time                        (env RAMPUP_SECONDS) default 1
  loops          iterations per user                 (env LOOP_COUNT)     default 5
  maxResponseMs  per-request SLO for the list reads  (env MAX_RESPONSE_MS) default 10000
  domain / port / protocol / env   target service (injected by entrypoint.sh)

NOTE: the perf suite proves the SIZE/LATENCY delta. The functional acceptance
criteria (payload excludes the document body, includes has_baseline) belong in
the backend integration tests, not here.</stringProp>
      <elementProp name="TestPlan.user_defined_variables" elementType="Arguments" guiclass="ArgumentsPanel" testclass="Arguments" testname="User Defined Variables">
        <collectionProp name="Arguments.arguments">
          <elementProp name="maxResponseMs" elementType="Argument">
            <stringProp name="Argument.name">maxResponseMs</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.value">${__P(maxResponseMs,${__env(MAX_RESPONSE_MS,10000)})}</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.metadata">=</stringProp>
          </elementProp>
          <elementProp name="userId" elementType="Argument">
            <stringProp name="Argument.name">userId</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.value">${__P(userId,${__env(USER_ID,perf-user)})}</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Argument.metadata">=</stringProp>
          </elementProp>
        </collectionProp>
      </elementProp>
    </TestPlan>
    <hashTree>
      <HeaderManager guiclass="HeaderPanel" testclass="HeaderManager" testname="Auth + JSON headers">
        <collectionProp name="HeaderManager.headers">
          <elementProp name="" elementType="Header">
            <stringProp name="Header.name">Authorization</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Header.value">Bearer ${__P(token,${__env(TOKEN,)})}</stringProp>
          </elementProp>
          <elementProp name="" elementType="Header">
            <stringProp name="Header.name">Content-Type</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="Header.value">application/json</stringProp>
          </elementProp>
        </collectionProp>
      </HeaderManager>
      <hashTree/>
      <ConfigTestElement guiclass="HttpDefaultsGui" testclass="ConfigTestElement" testname="HTTP Request Defaults (backend)">
        <stringProp name="HTTPSampler.protocol">${__P(protocol, https)}</stringProp>
        <stringProp name="HTTPSampler.domain">${__P(domain, bng-metric-backend.${__P(env)}.cdp-int.defra.cloud)}</stringProp>
        <stringProp name="HTTPSampler.port">${__P(port, 443)}</stringProp>
        <elementProp name="HTTPsampler.Arguments" elementType="Arguments" guiclass="HTTPArgumentsPanel" testclass="Arguments" testname="User Defined Variables">
          <collectionProp name="Arguments.arguments"/>
        </elementProp>
      </ConfigTestElement>
      <hashTree/>
      <SetupThreadGroup guiclass="SetupThreadGroupGui" testclass="SetupThreadGroup" testname="Seed projects (setUp)">
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.num_threads">1</stringProp>
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.ramp_time">1</stringProp>
        <boolProp name="ThreadGroup.same_user_on_next_iteration">true</boolProp>
        <stringProp name="ThreadGroup.on_sample_error">continue</stringProp>
        <elementProp name="ThreadGroup.main_controller" elementType="LoopController" guiclass="LoopControlPanel" testclass="LoopController" testname="Loop Controller">
          <stringProp name="LoopController.loops">${__P(seedProjects,${__env(SEED_PROJECTS,10)})}</stringProp>
          <boolProp name="LoopController.continue_forever">false</boolProp>
        </elementProp>
      </SetupThreadGroup>
      <hashTree>
        <HTTPSamplerProxy guiclass="HttpTestSampleGui" testclass="HTTPSamplerProxy" testname="POST /projects/new (seed baseline)">
          <stringProp name="HTTPSampler.path">/projects/new</stringProp>
          <boolProp name="HTTPSampler.follow_redirects">true</boolProp>
          <stringProp name="HTTPSampler.method">POST</stringProp>
          <boolProp name="HTTPSampler.use_keepalive">true</boolProp>
          <boolProp name="HTTPSampler.postBodyRaw">true</boolProp>
          <elementProp name="HTTPsampler.Arguments" elementType="Arguments">
            <collectionProp name="Arguments.arguments">
              <elementProp name="" elementType="HTTPArgument">
                <boolProp name="HTTPArgument.always_encode">false</boolProp>
                <stringProp name="Argument.value">${seedBody}</stringProp>
                <stringProp name="Argument.metadata">=</stringProp>
              </elementProp>
            </collectionProp>
          </elementProp>
        </HTTPSamplerProxy>
        <hashTree>
          <JSR223PreProcessor guiclass="TestBeanGUI" testclass="JSR223PreProcessor" testname="Build baseline body">
            <stringProp name="scriptLanguage">groovy</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="cacheKey">true</stringProp>
            <stringProp name="script">import groovy.json.JsonBuilder

// Number of synthetic parcels in this project's baseline document. -JseedParcels
// wins, then the CDP env var SEED_PARCELS, then the default. Bigger = bigger
// JSONB doc = the exact cost this baseline is measuring.
int parcels = (props.get('seedParcels') ?: System.getenv('SEED_PARCELS') ?: '500') as int
int iter = vars.getIteration()

def habitats = []
parcels.times { i -&gt;
  // Only featureId (uuid) and status are schema-required; the rest are filled to
  // approximate a realistic ~few-KB-per-parcel document rather than a bare row.
  habitats.add([
    featureId: UUID.randomUUID().toString(),
    ref: 'P-' + i,
    type: 'Lowland meadows',
    broadType: 'Grassland',
    distinctiveness: 'High',
    distinctivenessScore: 6,
    condition: 'Good',
    conditionScore: 3,
    strategicSignificance: 'Formally identified in local strategy',
    retentionCategory: 'Retained',
    area: 1234,
    sizeSquareMetres: 1234.56,
    status: 'Complete',
    units: 7.89,
    siteName: 'Perf Test Site',
    surveyDate: '2024-01-01',
    surveyDetails: 'Synthetic parcel generated for the BMD-933 baseline perf test',
    mappedBy: 'perf-bot',
    company: 'Perf Co',
    baseMap: 'OS MasterMap',
    properties: [ ParcelRef: 'P-' + i, HabitatType: 'Lowland meadows', BroadHabitat: 'Grassland', Condition: 'Good', AreaSqm: 1234 ]
  ])
}

// name is unique per seeded project so repeat runs never collide.
def doc = [ project: [ name: 'perf-' + System.nanoTime() + '-' + iter, baseline: [ habitats: habitats ] ] ]
vars.put('seedBody', new JsonBuilder(doc).toString())</stringProp>
          </JSR223PreProcessor>
          <hashTree/>
          <ResponseAssertion guiclass="AssertionGui" testclass="ResponseAssertion" testname="Created (2xx)">
            <collectionProp name="Asserion.test_strings">
              <stringProp name="46817057">^20[01]$</stringProp>
            </collectionProp>
            <stringProp name="Assertion.test_field">Assertion.response_code</stringProp>
            <boolProp name="Assertion.assume_success">false</boolProp>
            <intProp name="Assertion.test_type">1</intProp>
          </ResponseAssertion>
          <hashTree/>
        </hashTree>
      </hashTree>
      <ThreadGroup guiclass="ThreadGroupGui" testclass="ThreadGroup" testname="GET /projects (list)">
